  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat overtime multiplier applies to Mark's weekend work? Mark used to make $11 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 1; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nWhat overtime multiplier applies to Mark's weekend work? Mark used to make $11 per hour.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"1. Overtime pay is commonly calculated at **time-and-a-half**.\\n2. “Time-and-a-half” means the regular wage is multiplied by \\\\(1.5\\\\).\\n3. Mark’s former wage of \\\\$11 per hour affects the pay amount, but not the multip...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Mark used to make $10 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Overtime is commonly paid at **time-and-a-half**, meaning the regular hourly wage is multiplied by \\(1.5\\). Mark’s wage of \\$10 per hour changes the overtime pay amount, not the multiplier.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1.5\\times}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much would Mark earn for an 8-hour regular workday? Additionally, Mark works 8 regular hours in a standard weekday shift.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark earns his regular rate of \\$10 per hour for 8 hours:\n\n\\[\n8 \\times \\$10 = \\$80\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$80}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Mark works 8 hours a day for 6 days a week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark works:\n\n\\[\n8 \\text{ hours/day} \\times 6 \\text{ days} = 48 \\text{ hours/week}\n\\]\n\nAt \\$10 per hour:\n\n- **First 40 hours:** \\(40 \\times \\$10 = \\$400\\)\n- **Overtime hours:** \\(48-40=8\\) hours\n- **Overtime rate:** \\(1.5 \\times \\$10 = \\$15\\) per hour\n- **Overtime pay:** \\(8 \\times \\$15 = \\$120\\)\n\nThus, assuming overtime begins after 40 hours per week:\n\n\\[\n\\$400+\\$120=\\boxed{\\$520\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nIf all 48 hours are paid at the regular rate, the total would instead be \\$480.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How much money does Mark make in one week? One more thing you should know: Mark's pay was raised by $2 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s new regular wage is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{/hour}\n\\]\n\nHe works \\(48\\) hours per week:\n\n- Regular pay: \\(40 \\times \\$12 = \\$480\\)\n- Overtime rate: \\(1.5 \\times \\$12 = \\$18\\text{/hour}\\)\n- Overtime pay: \\(8 \\times \\$18 = \\$144\\)\n\nTotal weekly pay:\n\n\\[\n\\$480+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$624}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Mark's employer pays 1.5 times the regular hourly rate for weekend work.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s raised regular rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{/hour}\n\\]\n\nAssuming his 6-day schedule includes **one 8-hour weekend day**, those weekend hours are paid at \\(1.5\\) times his regular rate:\n\n\\[\n\\$12 \\times 1.5=\\$18\\text{/hour}\n\\]\n\nWeekly earnings:\n\n- \\(40\\) regular hours: \\(40 \\times \\$12=\\$480\\)\n- \\(8\\) weekend/overtime hours: \\(8 \\times \\$18=\\$144\\)\n\n\\[\n\\$480+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$624\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nThis assumes the weekend premium and overtime rate are the same \\(1.5\\times\\) rate, rather than being compounded.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Mark works 8 hours a day for 5 days a week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s new regular rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{/hour}\n\\]\n\nHe works:\n\n\\[\n8 \\times 5=40\\text{ hours per week}\n\\]\n\nAssuming **one of those five days is a weekend day**:\n\n- Regular weekday pay: \\(32 \\times \\$12=\\$384\\)\n- Weekend pay: \\(8 \\times (1.5 \\times \\$12)=8 \\times \\$18=\\$144\\)\n\n\\[\n\\$384+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$528\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nIf all five workdays are weekdays, he would earn \\(\\$480\\) per week.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
